<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aceh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aceh is the northernmost province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, at the tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banda-aceh">Banda Aceh</a>. From the 16th century it was the seat of the Aceh Sultanate, a leading Muslim power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>, which resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh-war">Aceh War</a> from 1873. After decades of separatist conflict and the 2004 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> tsunami, a peace agreement in 2005 gave the province special autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aceh.jpg" alt="Aceh" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aceh_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
